# Copy to .dev.vars and fill in. Never commit .dev.vars.
# Each provider is optional — the waterfall skips any vendor with no key and
# records "unconfigured" in the attempt ledger so you can see the gap.
#
# One key per vendor, entered once, serves every waterfall it can. Fourteen of
# these vendors also resolve the COMPANY behind a lead (industry, HQ, LinkedIn
# page, ticker) from the same key — see "Company waterfall" in the README.
# Five have no company API at all: Skrapp, Anymail Finder, Zeliq, Dropcontact
# and Kaspr.

FINDYMAIL_API_KEY=
LEADMAGIC_API_KEY=
PROSPEO_API_KEY=
WIZA_API_KEY=
PEOPLEDATALABS_API_KEY=
CONTACTOUT_API_KEY=
HUNTER_API_KEY=
APOLLO_API_KEY=
ANYMAILFINDER_API_KEY=
SKRAPP_API_KEY=
DATAGMA_API_KEY=
SURFE_API_KEY=
ROCKETREACH_API_KEY=
KASPR_API_KEY=
DROPCONTACT_API_KEY=
ZELIQ_API_KEY=

# Three vendors need more than one opaque token, so their secrets are compound:
#   Forager puts the account id in the URL path.
FORAGER_API_KEY=accountId:apiKey
#   Tomba authenticates with two headers, X-Tomba-Key and X-Tomba-Secret.
TOMBA_API_KEY=key:secret
#   Snov.io uses OAuth client credentials (API User ID + API Secret from
#   app.snov.io/account/api); the app mints the bearer token itself.
SNOV_API_KEY=clientId:clientSecret

# Buying a key is not always the same as unlocking the API. Two to watch:
#   Wiza     — plan credits (email/phone) and API credits are separate pools.
#              A paid plan alone leaves /individual_reveals failing with
#              fail_error "billing_issue"; the API draws on API credits, bought
#              separately under Settings → API.
#   LeadMagic — no API access on the free tier at all; a key can only be minted
#              on an active paid plan.
#   Apollo   — the key works on the free plan, for companies as well as people,
#              which makes it the one company vendor you can try for nothing. Phone numbers are delivered to
#              a webhook minutes later, so the phone field pauses the lead
#              until Apollo calls back (see README, "Vendors that answer later").
#   Snov.io  — no API access on the Trial plan; Starter and up. Its company
#              lookup bills per REQUEST rather than per match, so a domain it
#              cannot resolve still costs a credit — which is why it is last in
#              the default company order.
#   Surfe    — the API is listed on the Enterprise plan only.
#   Kaspr    — API access from the Starter plan; the free plan is "limited".
#   Dropcontact, Zeliq — answer by callback only. They cannot deliver to a
#              local `pnpm dev`, so on a laptop they are skipped with an error
#              that says so; they run once the app is deployed.
